  "description": "1.  Leyland cypress (conifer near the garden gate) - reduce width on the gate side and front (not left side).\r2. Cotoneaster frigidus  (between flowering cherry tree and silver birch) ? reduce so branches don?t overhang oval bed.\r3. Flowering cherry tree (Warwick Avenue end) - reduce back to most recent reduction points \r4. Two large Leyland cypress ? reduce height to level of adjacent mews roof & take back branches in line with lawn border to allow more light to flower bed.\r5. Ilex aquifolium (holly) - cut half off top to make it small compact tree\r6. Sambucus nigra - pollard (near Castellain road)\r7. Sycamore (left side of electricity sub-station) Reduce branches above public footpath by up to 3 meters and prune back to boundary\r8. Sycamore (right side of electricity sub-station) crown reduce back to previous, most recent reduction points\r9. x2 laurus nobilis trees - to reduce width to give light to the shrubs underneath \r10. 5x  London plane trees - reduce back to most recent reduction points \r11. x2 lime trees - reduce back to most recent reduction points l\r13. sycamores opp 127/129 crown reduce back to most recent points \r\rThese trees have been seen by Rosie Dobson earlier in the year",
